WEBVTT

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:10.990
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Thursday the twentieth. Can you all hear me, or am I talking to myself again?</v>

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:18.339
<v Callum Reid>We can hear you. Sadly, nothing from the broken coffee machine in the canteen. Absolutely dead.</v>

00:00:20.719 --> 00:00:24.219
<v Jamie Brennan>Probably heard what we call its coffee and taken offence.</v>

00:00:26.519 --> 00:00:32.469
<v Callum Reid>And the heating in the portakabin is on. In August. Lovely combination, no coffee and gently roasting.</v>

00:00:34.630 --> 00:00:37.079
<v Marcus Hale>That's your luxury office package, that is.</v>

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:44.920
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, neither of those is going on this engineering list. Before the live jobs, a few things that are already closed.</v>

00:00:46.039 --> 00:00:52.689
<v Sarah Okafor>I signed off the inspection on the boiler safety valve on Tuesday. That's done, not something we're allocating again.</v>

00:00:53.259 --> 00:00:57.460
<v David Whitfield>Same here, signed off the inspection on the old turbine on Tuesday.</v>

00:00:59.179 --> 00:01:06.530
<v David Whitfield>But for any further access, I can't get to the old turbine until production gives us a window. That's still blocked.</v>

00:01:07.609 --> 00:01:12.510
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. Completed inspection stays completed; further access is blocked, no new job agreed there.</v>

00:01:13.739 --> 00:01:20.739
<v Jamie Brennan>And I already swapped the filter on the power pack on one yesterday. Just so that doesn't get dragged forward.</v>

00:01:21.230 --> 00:01:24.730
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, different filter from the one we're about to discuss.</v>

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:27.829
<v Jamie Brennan>Exactly. The power pack on one is done.</v>

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:36.590
<v Callum Reid>Only other thing from nights: noticed the big valve by the gate was running a bit warm on nights but it settled down.</v>

00:01:38.129 --> 00:01:43.030
<v Grace Liu>Settled back down, yeah? You're flagging an observation, not asking for work on it?</v>

00:01:43.930 --> 00:01:48.129
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, just an observation. Nothing being added off the back of that.</v>

00:01:50.549 --> 00:01:55.450
<v Olumide Adeyemi>And the shutdown on the turbine two is cancelled now, production need it running.</v>

00:01:56.969 --> 00:02:01.519
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, cancelled. Keep that out of the actions. Let's do the actual priorities.</v>

00:02:02.319 --> 00:02:09.669
<v Sarah Okafor>Haley, can you swap the filter on the CT1 tomorrow at 9:30? That's holding production up so it needs doing first.</v>

00:02:11.969 --> 00:02:15.819
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, I'll swap the filter on the CT1 tomorrow at 9:30.</v>

00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:20.699
<v Callum Reid>That's the production hold-up, yes. Not the power pack filter Jamie's already done.</v>

00:02:22.139 --> 00:02:25.289
<v Marcus Hale>Got you. CT1 gets done first, that's my priority.</v>

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:32.780
<v Sarah Okafor>Then we've got the vibration readings on the front end of one. Who's able to take that?</v>

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:39.639
<v Olumide Adeyemi>I'll take vibration readings on the front end of one by 11am. It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:43.550
<v Marcus Hale>Just the readings, then, not pulling anything apart?</v>

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:50.710
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, just taking the vibration readings. That's what I'm putting my hand up for.</v>

00:02:52.229 --> 00:02:53.979
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Mide. By 11am, agreed.</v>

00:02:55.069 --> 00:03:02.419
<v Sarah Okafor>Dave, can you book a contractor to look at the turbine one compressor by Thursday? It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:03:04.169 --> 00:03:09.419
<v David Whitfield>Yeah, um, booking made by Thursday, rather than having the contractor physically here by Thursday?</v>

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:18.689
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly, book them by Thursday, which is today. We're not setting their visit date here. It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:25.650
<v David Whitfield>Understood. I'll book a contractor to look at the turbine one compressor by Thursday.</v>

00:03:27.259 --> 00:03:32.860
<v Jamie Brennan>Good distinction. A booking and someone actually turning up with a van are very different things.</v>

00:03:33.189 --> 00:03:36.689
<v David Whitfield>Especially once you've enjoyed twenty minutes of their hold music.</v>

00:03:38.789 --> 00:03:43.340
<v Sarah Okafor>Mide, can you chase the purchase order for the water booster after lunch?</v>

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:48.319
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, I'll chase the purchase order for the water booster after lunch.</v>

00:03:50.449 --> 00:03:57.449
<v Jamie Brennan>Water booster, yeah. That's separate from the filter I've just mentioned. Easy to muddle them when everyone's talking at once.</v>

00:03:58.770 --> 00:04:03.319
<v Sarah Okafor>And Olumide, can you inspect the feed pump for leaks? That's fairly important.</v>

00:04:05.669 --> 00:04:09.520
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yep, I'll inspect the feed pump for leaks. Fairly important, understood.</v>

00:04:10.229 --> 00:04:15.479
<v Marcus Hale>Sorry, spoke over you there. That one's a leak inspection, separate from the vibration readings?</v>

00:04:15.819 --> 00:04:22.120
<v Olumide Adeyemi>That's right. The feed pump for leaks; the front end of one for vibration readings. Two separate jobs.</v>

00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:31.040
<v Sarah Okafor>Mide, can I give you the shift handover report as well—send the shift handover report round by end of day?</v>

00:04:32.050 --> 00:04:40.100
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Sorry, no, I can't take that as well. With the readings, the feed pump and the purchase order chase, I'd be stretching it.</v>

00:04:40.439 --> 00:04:47.790
<v Sarah Okafor>Fair enough. Safety—sorry, safety Grace, can you take that instead and send the shift handover report round by end of day?</v>

00:04:49.990 --> 00:04:56.290
<v Grace Liu>Yes, I'll take it instead of Mide. I'll send the shift handover report round by end of day.</v>

00:04:56.839 --> 00:05:02.790
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks. And safety Grace, can you organise the toolbox talk for the team for tomorrow? Normal priority.</v>

00:05:04.660 --> 00:05:09.910
<v Grace Liu>Yep, I'll organise the toolbox talk for the team for tomorrow. Normal priority, that's fine.</v>

00:05:10.399 --> 00:05:14.250
<v Callum Reid>Toolbox talk without canteen coffee. You'll have a very quiet audience.</v>

00:05:15.180 --> 00:05:19.379
<v Grace Liu>Quiet would be a first. But yes, organising that one's with me.</v>

00:05:21.069 --> 00:05:28.769
<v Callum Reid>There's the big board as well. Mide, can you run a function test on the big board first thing tomorrow? Low priority.</v>

00:05:30.279 --> 00:05:36.230
<v Olumide Adeyemi>No, sorry, I can't take that one on as well. Need to leave that with someone else.</v>

00:05:38.310 --> 00:05:45.660
<v Callum Reid>Okay. David Whitfield, could you take it instead? Run a function test on the big board first thing tomorrow, low priority.</v>

00:05:46.339 --> 00:05:52.290
<v David Whitfield>Yes, I'll take that instead. I'll run a function test on the big board first thing tomorrow.</v>

00:05:53.129 --> 00:05:59.079
<v Sarah Okafor>And we're keeping that low priority. The timing's agreed, but we're not calling it a production emergency.</v>

00:05:59.649 --> 00:06:01.050
<v David Whitfield>Yeah, low priority. Understood.</v>

00:06:03.069 --> 00:06:08.319
<v Marcus Hale>Whereas the CT1 filter is the one holding production up. Just keeping those two straight.</v>

00:06:09.500 --> 00:06:15.100
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. Haley's CT1 filter tomorrow at 9:30 needs doing first. Different urgency from the big board.</v>

00:06:16.490 --> 00:06:22.790
<v Grace Liu>Just checking mine haven't blurred together: shift handover report round by end of day, toolbox talk for tomorrow.</v>

00:06:23.819 --> 00:06:27.319
<v Sarah Okafor>Correct, safety Grace. And the toolbox talk is normal priority.</v>

00:06:29.310 --> 00:06:37.709
<v Jamie Brennan>And no repeat of the power pack filter. Sorry, banging on about it, but I don't fancy seeing yesterday's finished job come back round.</v>

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:40.870
<v Sarah Okafor>No repeat. That one's closed.</v>

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:45.860
<v Callum Reid>Unlike the coffee machine discussion, which will apparently run forever.</v>

00:06:47.660 --> 00:06:49.759
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Low output, high vibration. Sounds familiar.</v>

00:06:50.079 --> 00:06:51.829
<v Marcus Hale>That's just Callum before breakfast.</v>

00:06:53.379 --> 00:06:56.879
<v Callum Reid>Cheers. Knew there was a reason I joined these calls.</v>

00:06:57.689 --> 00:07:02.589
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before this becomes a condition report on Callum—everyone clear on what they've accepted?</v>

00:07:03.589 --> 00:07:04.790
<v David Whitfield>Yep, clear here.</v>

00:07:05.850 --> 00:07:07.050
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, all clear.</v>

00:07:07.889 --> 00:07:09.089
<v Grace Liu>Same here.</v>

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:12.560
<v Marcus Hale>Yep.</v>

00:07:13.269 --> 00:07:18.519
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely. That's the agreed list, nothing added for the blocked or cancelled work. Thanks, everyone.</v>
